The miRBase Sequence Database -- Release 23.1 (Sep 2026)
--------------------------------------------------------

1. SUMMARY

The miRBase database provides a searchable online repository for
published microRNA sequences and associated annotation. miRBase also
provides a gene naming and nomenclature function.

Release 23.1 of the database contains 46603 entries representing hairpin
precursor miRNAs, expressing 74463 mature miRNA products, in 323
species. The data are freely available to all through the web
interface at http://www.mirbase.org/.


2. CHANGES SINCE RELEASE 23

589 misannotated hairpin sequences and 1078 mature sequences have been
deleted from the database. 6 hairpin sequences and 9 mature sequences
have been renamed. 2 mature entries have had their sequences
changed. See the miRNA.diff file for the full description of changes.


2.1 CHANGES BETWEEN RELEASE 22 and 23

8847 new hairpin sequences and 27005 new mature products have been
added. The first miRNAs in 47 new species are reported.

20514 mature sequences have had their names clarified, usually upon
the addition of a 2nd mature product from the same locus. For example,
hsa-miR-107 is renamed to hsa-miR-107-3p on the addition of
hsa-miR-107-5p to the database.

The sequences of 9091 mature products have changed, the overwhelming
number of which have had their 5' or 3' ends adjusted based on large
scale small RNA deep sequencing data.

244 misannotated hairpin sequences, and 361 mature sequences sequences
have been deleted from the database.


3. FILES

The following files are available for download from the website:

  hairpin.fa    - predicted miR stem-loop sequences in fasta format
  mature.fa     - mature sequences in fasta format
  miRNA.dead    - entries removed from the database
  miRNA.diff    - differences between the current and last release

The genomes/ directory contains gff files of genome coordinates for 31
species. See the individual files for the genome assemblies used.


